From: Nate White <nate@nexthop.ai>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 16:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: aspeed: fblite-r1: add BIOS flash on SPI1 CS1

The CPU BIOS SPI flash is reachable from the BMC on SPI1 chip-select 1
(behind the CPU FPGA mux). Add a jedec,spi-nor node for it so it shows
up as an MTD device, and enable the SPI1CS1 pin group.

SPI1 on the AST2620 sits on the GPIOZ strap pins, which carry internal
pull-downs on A2/A3 silicon (SCU638[15:8]). Together with the external
4.7k strap pull-down, the one on GPIOZ5 (SPI1 MISO, ball AA11) loads the
level-translated MISO from the CPU card enough to corrupt every array
read of the BIOS flash while RDID still succeeds. Add a bias-disable
pinconf for the SPI1 pins to the spi1 pinctrl state. Straps are latched
at reset, before this applies, so strap values are unchanged. GPIOZ2
(WP#, AE10) is omitted: external pull-up, no pinconf entry in the driver.

Pin the flash node to single-IO, which is all the CPU FPGA mux passes,
and request fast read so the controller uses FAST_READ4B with dummy
cycles.

Co-authored-by: Jack Cai <jack@nexthop.ai>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-facebook-fblite-r1.dts | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-facebook-fblite-r1.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-facebook-fblite-r1.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-facebook-fblite-r1.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-facebook-fblite-r1.dts
@@ -119,3 +119,33 @@
 		spi-rx-bus-width = <1>;
 	};
 };
+
+&pinctrl {
+	/*
+	 * SPI1 sits on the GPIOZ strap pins, which carry internal pull-downs on
+	 * AST2620 A2/A3. They load the level-translated MISO from the CPU card
+	 * enough to corrupt BIOS flash reads. Straps are latched at reset, so
+	 * dropping the pull-downs afterwards is safe. GPIOZ2 (WP#, AE10) has
+	 * an external pull-up and no pinconf entry in the driver.
+	 */
+	pinctrl_spi1_nopd: spi1-nopd {
+		pins = "AC10", "AD10", "AB11", "AC11", "AA11", "AD11", "AF10";
+		bias-disable;
+	};
+};
+
+&spi1 {
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&pinctrl_spi1_default &pinctrl_spi1cs1_default &pinctrl_spi1_nopd>;
+
+	flash@1 {
+		status = "okay";
+		compatible = "jedec,spi-nor";
+		reg = <1>;
+		spi-max-frequency = <10000000>;
+		spi-tx-bus-width = <1>;
+		spi-rx-bus-width = <1>;
+		m25p,fast-read;
+		label = "bios";
+	};
+};
